{"title":"2018 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A jar contains 6 crayons, of which 3 are red, 2 are blue, and 1 is green. Jakob reaches into the jar and randomly removes 2 of the crayons. What is the probability that both of these crayons are red?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can label the crayons as R1, R2, R3, B1, B2, and G, where R1, R2, R3 represent red crayons, B1 and B2 represent blue crayons, and G represents the green crayon. We can also halve the number of crayon pairs we actually have to look through by considering swapped options as the same. For example, R1G and GR1 will be considered the same. The possible pairs are then:\n</p><p>R1R2, R1R3, R1B1, R1B2, R1G, R2R3, R2B1, R2B2, R2G, R3B1, R3B2, R3G, B1B2, B1G, B2G\n</p><p>Counting, we see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> pairs and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of them have two red crayons. Thus, the probability that both crayons are red would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43f332eb2535675cfb1470bde17fb5124bb3354.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{15} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"73\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> crayons and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> red crayons, there would initially be a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/a/66a739922bf84b691c95317eeedee9b628b5afac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{6} = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" /> probability of getting a red crayon. However, after removing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> crayon, there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> crayons and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> red crayons, so there would then be a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2297526ede0e6c616802ca72adf69c82518f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> probability of having the second crayon be red.\n</p><p>The probability that both of these crayons are red would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/266271abd0d663baa94e0a0f0baf651811df1afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{2}{5} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"99\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> crayons on the first crayon removed and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on the second, there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3baf0066ce7886d39f68ef8e6ac40747eaf9ca6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 5 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> possibilities (where order matters for each crayon).\n</p><p>Using similar logic, there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/8/e28d1e652b6dc015f8ca44794e86577f322810a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 2 = 6$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" /> possibilities where both crayons are red.\n</p><p>The probability that both crayons are red would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038a2a3a5db65e5ff577334f52d1eba1f6248f4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{30} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"73\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC\" title=\"2018 CSMC\">2018 CSMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2018 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2018 CSMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2018 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2018 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2018 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2018 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2018 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2018 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2018 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2018 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2\" title=\"2018 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2018 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Senior_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Senior Competition\">CEMC Senior Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018062018\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.061 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 136/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 134/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2892/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.502      1 Template:CEMC_CIMC/CSMC_box\n100.00%    7.502      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37283:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018062018 and revision id 287929. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}